<interrogationes unitas="registrum_commandi">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I add a new $command that a pagina tag can run?
    <responsum symbolum="registrum_commandi_registrare concha_registrare_commandi FunctioCommand">Write
      a FunctioCommand (b32 fn(ContextusCommandi* ctx), VERUM on
      success) and register it under its name with
      registrum_commandi_registrare(reg, "nomen", fn, datum). Inside
      concha use concha_registrare_commandi, which forwards to the
      same call. Widgets do it in their _init function (see
      libro_paginarum_init registering rename, goto and
      new).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how does a command handler get at the widget or state it belongs to?
    <responsum symbolum="registrum_commandi_executare ContextusCommandi" via="lib/libro_paginarum.c">Two
      pointers arrive in the ContextusCommandi.
      ctx->datum_registratus is the datum given at registration
      (widgets pass their ContextusWidget and cast it back);
      registrum_commandi_executare writes it into the context on every
      call, overwriting whatever the caller left there.
      ctx->datum_custom is per call site: layout.c passes the libro for
      a pagina inside a libro and NIHIL otherwise, and schirmata.c
      passes its libro. The context also carries the pagina, a
      piscina, and the grid line and column where the tag
      ends.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I tell "command not found" apart from "the command failed" when I execute one?
    <responsum symbolum="registrum_commandi_executare registrum_commandi_habet">Not
      from registrum_commandi_executare alone: it returns FALSUM for
      an unknown name and otherwise returns whatever the handler
      returned, so a handler that fails also gives FALSUM. Ask
      registrum_commandi_habet first when the difference
      matters.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I re-register a command name or remove a command?
    <responsum symbolum="registrum_commandi_registrare tabula_dispersa_inserere">Registering
      the same name again replaces the earlier handler and datum (the
      hash table overwrites the value; the old Command stays allocated
      in the piscina). There is no remove function. Registration
      returns nothing, so a refused registration is silent: a NIHIL
      registry, name or function returns early, and an empty name is
      refused by tabula_dispersa_inserere (key length zero) after the
      Command was already allocated. concha_registrare_commandi
      returns VERUM for those refusals too (FALSUM only when the
      concha or its registry is NIHIL).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I list every registered command, for help text or completion?
    <responsum symbolum="RegistrumCommandi registrum_commandi_habet tabula_dispersa_iterator_initium tabula_dispersa_iterator_proximum">Not
      through this API: the only query is registrum_commandi_habet for
      one name. The commands live in reg->tabula, a chorda-keyed
      TabulaDispersa whose values are Command pointers, so walking
      that table directly with tabula_dispersa_iterator_initium and
      tabula_dispersa_iterator_proximum is the only way today. Command.titulus keeps
      at most XXXI characters of the name, but lookup uses the full
      name.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
